<!-- ============================== HOW IT WORKS ============================== -->
<section class="section" id="how">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
      <h2 class="display h2">One receipt.<br/>Two states.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="steps reveal">
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">01 · POST</div>
        <h3>Send the HTTP receipt</h3>
        <p>Any runtime posts the same body. Use the ingest key, not an MCP key. The shell expands <code class="mono">$CRONTINEL_INGEST_KEY</code>.</p>
        <pre><span class="cmt"># Node. curl sends this same JSON.</span>
<span class="ok">status</span>: "completed"
<span class="ok">exit_code</span>: 0
<span class="bad">processed_records</span>: 0</pre>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">02 · CHECK</div>
        <h3>Exit 0 can still fail</h3>
        <p>The server keeps the process status. The outcome rule is separate. A minimum of 1 fails a zero count.</p>
        <pre><span class="ok">run</span>       completed · exit 0
<span class="bad">outcome</span>   failed · actual 0</pre>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <div class="n">03 · CLEAR</div>
        <h3>A later count closes it</h3>
        <p>The email goes out with the model off. A later receipt that passes the rule resolves the incident.</p>
        <pre><span class="ok">processed_records</span>  1
<span class="ok">outcome</span>            passed</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

